{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MolecularConstruction.IlpCovalentBond","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MolecularConstruction.IlpCovalentBond","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.bond_V3_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.bond_V3_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/ilp-covalent-bond.lean#L33-L37","doc":"**The γγ bond letter V³ is a γγ word**: three pair-production vertices at\nthe junction site `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.inverse_trefoil_not_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.inverse_trefoil_not_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/ilp-covalent-bond.lean#L27-L31","doc":"**The inverse trefoil is not a γγ word**: it has odd length, and every γγ\nword has even length (`gammaGamma_length_even`).  So under the one γγ rule it\ncannot be the H₂ bond word. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:ilp-covalent-bond","label":"prop:ilp-covalent-bond","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/ilp-covalent-bond.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.inverse_trefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.inverse_trefoil","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/ilp-covalent-bond.lean#L24-L25","doc":"The inverse trefoil braid word σ₀⁻¹σ₁⁻¹σ₀⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0}]}